    "chunk_text": "learned. Game theory describes the rational behavior of multiple interacting agents and is used in AI programs that make decisions that involve other agents.  Learning Machine learning is the study of programs that can improve their performance on a given task automatically. It has been a part of AI from the beginning.  There are several kinds of machine learning. Unsupervised learning analyzes a stream of data and finds patterns and makes predictions without any other guidance. Supervised learning requires labeling the training data with the expected answers, and comes in two main varieties: classification (where the program must learn to predict what category the input belongs in) and regression (where the program must deduce a numeric",
